ording\") and AC line \"With a recording OpenTelemetry span active, trace_id equals that span's trace id as 32 hex\"","norm_id":"nd642f24079a4f947","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Drop the live-span derivation: mint `secrets.token_hex(16)` unconditionally per gate run, and remove the corresponding 'with a recording span active, trace_id equals that span's trace id' acceptance criterion. This keeps the leaf a subset of the epic, whose out-of-scope section defers real-OTel-trace-id carriage to later work.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct the emitter citation: replace `completion_reconcile.py:252` with the real location (`gate_ops.py`, `completion_reconcile` step, trace_id at `:269`) and reconcile the claim that it 'stays None' with the fact that it carries `ctx.inputs.get(\"trace_id\")` through — the path the completion-verifier verdict AC depends on.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.75,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Other emitters run inside a gate scope with no LLM call (workflow/completion_verdict_assembly.py:153, completion_reconcile.py:252, workflow/completion_failures.py:98) ... all stay None and are out of scope'","search_files: no file `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_reconcile.py` exists; `completion_reconcile` is a step function at `gate_ops.py:251`","read_file gate_ops.py:252 is the step docstring; gate_ops.py:269 emits `\"trace_id\": ctx.inputs.get(\"trace_id\")` — a carry-through, not `None`","This reconcile step is the one that produces the completion-verifier verdict the plan's completion AC targets, so the exclusion both mislocates the file and misclassifies a carry-through path as a deterministic-null emitter"],"finding":"The plan asserts `completion_reconcile.py:252` is a deterministic emitter that 'stays None and is out of scope' because a deterministic verdict has no gateway request behind it, but there is no file `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_reconcile.py`; the `completion_reconcile` code is a step in `gate_ops.py` (def at :251, docstring at :252), and its actual trace_id emission at `gate_ops.py:269` is `ctx.inputs.get(\"trace_id\")` — a carry-through of the verify agent step's value, not a hardcoded null. The scope-exclusion premise is refuted by the code.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f42ab764fe005a06a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved wording paragraph: 'Other emitters run inside a gate scope with no LLM call (... completion_reconcile.py:252 ...); all stay None and are out of scope'","norm_id":"na86aab553f87f870","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author descopes gate_ops.py's completion_reconcile trace_id emission believing it is an out-of-scope deterministic null, but it is the exact carry path the completion-verifier verdict AC depends on","Implementer edits a nonexistent completion_reconcile.py:252 and cannot find the referenced emitter"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Drop `completion_reconcile.py:252` from the deterministic-null exclusion list; if the completion-verifier trace_id reaches the verdict via `gate_ops.py:269`'s `ctx.inputs.get(\"trace_id\")`, document that carry path (and how the structured runner's trace_id populates `ctx.inputs[\"trace_id\"]`) instead of describing it as an out-of-scope null.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the derive-vs-mint rationale with the mint TIMING: either (a) drop the span-derivation and always mint (since rebar's own spans are created downstream and get independent trace ids, the 'unify the header with exported spans' benefit is unreachable without also seeding the OTel context), or (b) additionally start/propagate a run-level span at the boundary carrying the minted id so downstream exported spans actually inherit it — and state which.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tracing.py:89/183: candidate_span opened per-`request` inside the runner's LLM call (downstream of the boundary)","tracing.py:226: Agent.instrument_all() — pydantic-ai spans created inside Agent.run, also downstream","gate_dispatch.py:167/:762: mint happens before gate_config(cfg) / run_workflow, i.e. before any run span is recording","Plan Scope/Approach never opens a boundary span nor sets the OTel trace context to the minted id; it only stores it on LLMConfig and emits it on the verdict/header","Plan concedes: 'Minting is the fallback when no span is recording, which is the common case today'"],"finding":"The stated derive-vs-mint rationale is not achievable by the plan's mechanism: trace_id is derived from an 'active OpenTelemetry span' AT THE BOUNDARY (gate_dispatch.py:167/:762), but rebar's own spans (candidate_span, tracing.py:183) and pydantic-ai's instrumented Agent spans are created DOWNSTREAM inside the LLM call, so no run-span is recording at mint time; and the plan never seeds the OTel trace context with the minted id, so downstream exported spans still get independent trace ids. The header/verdict id therefore will not unify with rebar's own exported spans in the very configuration the rationale invokes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f65772150b7b27a5f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section — 'the ACTIVE OpenTelemetry span's trace id when one is recording' / 'an unrelated random id would put a different id on the gateway header than on the exported spans for the same run'","norm_id":"n4037ba5456586fb8","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["[tracing] + LANGFUSE_* configured: header/verdict trace_id ≠ the trace_id of rebar's exported candidate/Agent spans for the same run, so Langfuse still shows two disjoint identities — the exact split the rationale claims to prevent","No external parent span (the common rebar case): the 'derive' branch never fires, so the whole derive path is effectively dead code justified by an unreachable benefit"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"If span-unification is not a real goal today, simplify to always `secrets.token_hex(16)` and remove the active-span derivation claim (and its AC). If unification IS the goal, add a boundary step that opens a run-level OTel span (or sets the trace context) using the minted id so pydantic-ai/candidate spans inherit it, and derive/mint accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"cd75495d609e7b1e","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f3472bf114ffe1b9",7936],"description_boxes":["38efaf2b16858416",0],"file_impact":["f7a2c5e7775e3b35",4],"ticket_id":["a7bc80678eef5681",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":5816.0,"input_tokens":862288,"llm_calls":30,"llm_ms":271983.0,"output_tokens":34564,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":288962.3,"verify_requests":14},"m